Version 0.1 (interim) — 2026-09-26. A final version is under legal review; this is not legal advice.

This file is the current licence for the pum suite and its verifier service. Where it
refers to the service it is a commercial licence; where it refers to this repository it is a
publication notice. The verifier clients are published so you can verify without trusting us.

1. DEFINITIONS
"Service" — the verifier service: you submit an artefact, we verify it against a named
policy, and return a signed receipt. "Receipt" — a signed record of what was submitted and
verified; it proves provenance and integrity, not the real-world truth of the artefact.
"Doctrine" — our published operating rules; "Doctrine Hash" — their published hash.

2. GRANT
Subject to these terms you may use the Service to submit artefacts, receive receipts, verify
receipts, and integrate verification into your own products. The Service verifies only: it
has no execution, shell, file-access or agent capability, and grants none.

3. DOCTRINE-HASH BINDING (core condition)
This licence is valid only while the deployed Doctrine Hash equals a hash in our published
registry and the receipt's doctrine_hash matches it. A modified ruleset voids it
automatically, without notice. The condition is technical, not merely contractual.

4. RESTRICTIONS
You shall not: reverse engineer the Service to build or operate an autonomous agent; resell,
white-label or present our verification as your own; remove or alter Doctrine hashes;
misrepresent verification results; or use the Service to harm people, gain unauthorised
access, deceive, conduct unlawful surveillance, develop weapons, or evade legal duties.

5. KEYS, QUOTAS, DATA
Keys are your responsibility; notify us of compromise. Per-plan quotas apply; payload cap is
currently 64 KB. We process submission content to produce receipts, do not train models on
your data, and handle personal data under the data-protection law of our home jurisdiction
(a Data Processing Addendum is available). Retention and cross-border safeguards are as
agreed in your order.

6. FEES
Fees, currency and payment terms are as stated in your order.

7. AUDIT
A written compliance report may be requested annually; on-site audit only for cause, with
reasonable notice and confidentiality.

8. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY
All rights in the Service, Doctrine and receipt format remain with the licensor. The verifier
clients are published publicly so you can verify independently of us.

9. WARRANTY & LIABILITY
The Service is provided "as is", without warranty of fitness for a particular purpose. A
receipt evidences what was submitted and verified; it does not guarantee truth, legality or
non-infringement. Aggregate liability is capped at the fees paid in the prior 12 months; no
indirect or consequential liability.

10. TERM, TERMINATION & REVOCATION
Either party may terminate for material breach uncured after notice. Keys may be revoked for
misuse, key compromise, non-payment or a legal order; revocation is signed, append-only and
never silent. Receipts signed by a revoked key are flagged invalid by independent
verification. Clauses 3, 4, 8, 9 and 11 survive termination.

11. GOVERNING LAW
This licence is governed by the laws of the Licensor's home jurisdiction (stated in your
order). Disputes are subject to the competent courts there unless the parties agree in
writing to arbitration.

12. THIS REPOSITORY
This repository contains governance documentation and the published verifier scripts
(prove_it.py, verify.sh). No product source code is published. The documents are published
for transparency about how the system governs itself.
